{"name":"Love at First Sight","hex":"#e5a5b1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"love at first sight","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An instantaneous attraction."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love_at_first_sight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Love at first sight","blocks":[{"text":"Love at first sight is a personal experience and a common trope in creative works: a person or character feels an instant, extreme, and ultimately long-lasting romantic attraction for a stranger upon first seeing them. It has been described by poets and critics since the emergence of ancient Greece."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love_at_first_sight","wikidata":"Q2526635"},{"title":"Love at First Sight (1929 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Love at First Sight is a 1929 American musical comedy film directed by Edgar Lewis and starring Norman Foster, Suzanne Keener and Doris Rankin."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love_at_First_Sight_(1929_film)","wikidata":"Q25136583"},{"title":"Love at First Sight (Kylie Minogue song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Love at First Sight\" is a song recorded by Australian singer Kylie Minogue for her eighth studio album Fever (2001). It was written and produced by Richard \"Biff\" Stannard and Julian Gallagher, with additional writing by Minogue, Ash Howes, and Martin Harrington. The song was released as the third single from Fever on 3 June 2002 by Festival Mushroom, Parlophone and Capitol Records. Musically, \"Love at First Sight\" is a dance-pop and nu-disco song which, lyrically, describes the singer falling and believing in love at first sight."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7e/Kylie_Minogue_-_Love_at_First_Sight.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love_at_First_Sight_(Kylie_Minogue_song)","wikidata":"Q726638"},{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love","wikidata":"Q316"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Burne-jones_cophetua.jpg/500px-Burne-jones_cophetua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Burne-jones_cophetua.jpg/1280px-Burne-jones_cophetua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Burne-jones_cophetua.jpg/500px-Burne-jones_cophetua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"King Cophetua and the Beggar Maid, 1884, by Edward Burne-Jones, depicts an older tale of love at first sight.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABurne-jones_cophetua.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7e/Kylie_Minogue_-_Love_at_First_Sight.png/250px-Kylie_Minogue_-_Love_at_First_Sight.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7e/Kylie_Minogue_-_Love_at_First_Sight.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7e/Kylie_Minogue_-_Love_at_First_Sight.png/250px-Kylie_Minogue_-_Love_at_First_Sight.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARsz_love_at_first_sight.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/11/Kylie_Minogue_Love_at_First_Sight_Video